=========================================================
TYPE TRAITS (C++11/14/17)
Interview Notes
=========================================================

1. What are Type Traits?
========================

Type Traits are compile-time utilities that provide information about types
or transform types.

They allow templates to make decisions during compilation instead of runtime.

Header File

#include <type_traits>

---------------------------------------------------------

Why are Type Traits Needed?

Generic code often needs to know properties of a type.

Examples

• Is this type an integer?
• Is it a pointer?
• Is it const?
• Is it a reference?
• Are two types the same?

Instead of checking these at runtime, Type Traits perform the checks at
compile time.

