21. Interview Questions
=======================

Q1. What are Type Traits?

Compile-time utilities that inspect or transform types.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Which header file contains Type Traits?

#include <type_traits>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Are Type Traits compile-time or runtime?

Compile-time.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. What does std::is_same do?

Checks whether two types are identical.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. What does std::is_integral check?

Whether a type is an integral type.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. What does std::remove_reference do?

Removes the reference qualifier from a type.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q7. What does std::decay do?

Converts a type to its value type by removing references, cv-qualifiers,
and converting arrays/functions to pointers when passed by value.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q8. What is std::enable_if?

A compile-time mechanism that enables or disables template functions
based on a condition (SFINAE).

---------------------------------------------------------

Q9. What is std::conditional?

A compile-time if-else that selects one of two types.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q10. Why are Type Traits important?

• Generic programming

• Template metaprogramming

• Compile-time optimization

• Better type safety

